Hello,

The F statistics are based on observed and expected heterozygosity whereas the Phi statistics are derived from AMOVA, which partitions the variance from genetic distance. If you want F statistics, you can use the basic.stats() or wc() functions from hierfstat: https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/hierfstat/vignettes/hierfstat.html

Best,
Zhian

